Feature: Notes List Done-Flag Visibility
  As a user of the notes web app
  I want each note's done flag shown in the notes list, with done notes clearly marked
  So that I can tell at a glance which notes are completed and which are still outstanding

  Background:
    Given the notes list view is open in the web app
    And the notes list displays all notes together in a single list

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 — the literal core of the request: every row reflects its done flag
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The done flag is a boolean-like completed state already present on the note model and is not redefined by this work
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The web app has a single notes list view where all notes are displayed together, and the change applies there
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The notes list already receives the done flag in the data it fetches, so no API change is required
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Every note row reflects its done flag
    Given the list contains a note whose done flag is set and a note whose done flag is not set
    When the notes list renders
    Then each note row should reflect its own done flag
    And the done note should be presented as done
    And the not-done note should be presented as not done

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 — display-only change: title, ordering and other list behaviour are untouched
  @key-example
  Scenario: Showing the done flag does not alter other list behaviour
    Given the list contains several notes in a known order
    When the notes list renders with done flags shown
    Then each note's title should be unchanged
    And the notes should appear in the same order as before
    And no other list behaviour should change

  # Why: FEAT-PO-002 — the second half of the request: done notes are visually separable at a glance
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] Done notes remain in their current list position; no reordering or grouping of done notes is applied
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The done treatment is a combination of a 'Done' textual label and visually differentiated row styling
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Done notes are visually distinct from not-done notes
    Given the list contains a done note and a not-done note
    When the notes list renders
    Then the done note's row should be visually distinct from the not-done note's row
    And the contrast between the two states should be legible in a single scan of the list

  # Why: FEAT-PO-003 — 'clearly' must survive color-blindness and monochrome displays
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The non-color done cue is a textual 'Done' label rather than an icon
  @key-example
  Scenario: Done state is conveyed by a non-color cue as well as styling
    Given the list contains a done note
    When the notes list renders
    Then the done note's row should carry a non-color done cue in addition to its styling
    And the done cue should be present on every done row

  # Why: FEAT-PO-003 — the non-color cue must be legible to screen readers and text-rendering contexts
  @key-example
  Scenario: A non-color textual cue conveys the done state alongside styling
    Given the list contains a done note
    When the notes list renders
    Then the done note's textual done cue should be readable as text
    And a screen reader should be able to announce the done cue's text

  # Why: FEAT-PO-004 — screen-reader users must hear the done state when navigating the list
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The done state is exposed to assistive technology via an accessible label or ARIA state on the row or its done indicator
  @key-example
  Scenario: Screen reader announces the done state of each row
    Given the list contains a done note and a not-done note
    When a screen reader user navigates the notes list
    Then the done note's row should be announced as done
    And the not-done note's row should be announced as not done

  # Why: FEAT-PO-001 — the not-done presentation is the default for every non-done row
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] A note whose done flag is unset or null is treated as not-done and rendered in the not-done presentation
  @boundary
  Scenario Outline: Rows render in the not-done presentation when the flag is not set
